<div class="sect">the model, line by line</div>
<p>This is the Scenarios sheet of the workbook, values as computed, so the whole argument fits on one screen: ten levers on top (the yellow cells), everything below them a formula. The DCF sheet does the same chain year by year; the Monte Carlo draws the levers from distributions and runs it {{n_runs_words}} times.</p>
{{table:scenarios}}
<p class="src">From IP_valuation_model.xlsx → Scenarios. Levers are judgments; derived rows are arithmetic. The Dictionary sheet in the workbook defines every term.</p>
